4.10.4 Handling Exception in JavaScript
There’s a syntax construct try...catch that allows us to “catch” errors so the script
can, instead of dying, do something more reasonable.
The “try…catch” syntax
The try...catch construct has two main blocks: try, and then catch:
try {
// code...
} catch (err) {
// error handling
}

